---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
---

<PolicyLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
	updated="August 14, 2026"
	description="How Sky House Cleaning collects, uses, and protects your personal information."
>
	<p>
		Sky House Cleaning ("we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This policy explains what
		information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have —
		whether you're booking a residential or commercial service, browsing our website, requesting
		a quote, or reaching out with a question. It applies to our website and to the booking,
		scheduling, and customer-management tools we use to run the business.
	</p>

	<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>When you book a service, request a quote, or contact us, we collect the information you provide directly, such as:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Your name, email address, and phone number</li>
		<li>Your home, business, or job-site address</li>
		<li>Vehicle details, if you're booking interior car detailing (year, make, model, color)</li>
		<li>Entry/access instructions, gate or alarm codes, electrical access notes, pet information, and any other notes you share about your appointment</li>
		<li>
			For commercial cleaning, post-construction cleaning, and garage cleaning &amp; organization —
			services we quote individually rather than price online — the scope details, quoted total,
			and any notes exchanged while putting the quote together
		</li>
		<li>Any messages, notes, or details you give us over the phone, by email, or through the website</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not collect or store your full payment card details. Payment is handled directly by
		Stripe, our payment processor (see "Third-Party Services" below). If you sign up for a
		recurring cleaning plan or membership, Stripe securely retains a payment method on file so we
		can bill each cleaning automatically — we never see or store the card number ourselves.
	</p>

	<h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
	<p>We use the information you provide to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Schedule, confirm, reschedule, and perform the cleaning, detailing, organization, or commercial service you've booked</li>
		<li>Calculate and collect payment, including recurring membership billing and deposits on quote-based jobs</li>
		<li>Assign the job to a cleaner or crew and give them what they need to complete it (name, address, access notes, timing)</li>
		<li>Communicate with you about your appointment — confirmations, reminders, invoices, and follow-ups</li>
		<li>Keep internal records of your service history so we can serve you consistently over time</li>
		<li>Respond to questions, quote requests, or other messages you send us</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We don't sell your personal information, and we don't use it for advertising or share it with data brokers.</p>

	<h2>Who Within Our Business Sees Your Information</h2>
	<p>
		We limit what each part of our team can see to what they actually need to do their job:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Cleaners and crews</strong> assigned to your job can see the job's schedule, address,
			access notes, and any service notes — what they need to get the work done. They do not have
			access to payment amounts, quoted totals, or deposit information for the job, regardless of
			what calendar access they're given.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Office/admin staff</strong> (currently just the owner) can see the full customer
			record — contact details, service history, pricing, and payment status — to run scheduling,
			billing, and customer service.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
	<p>We rely on a handful of outside services to run our booking, scheduling, and customer-management process. Each has its own privacy practices governing how it handles data, and we encourage you to review them if you'd like more detail:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Stripe</strong>: processes payments and, for recurring plans, stores your payment method securely to bill future cleanings. We don't see or store your full card number. See <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>Google Calendar</strong>: used to schedule and manage appointment times. If you provide an email address, Google Calendar may send you calendar invites and update emails directly for your appointment.</li>
		<li><strong>Google Firebase / Google Cloud (Firestore)</strong>: our internal customer-record and job-dispatch database, used to store contact information, service history, and job assignment status.</li>
		<li><strong>Google Places API / Google Business Profile</strong>: powers the customer reviews shown on our Reviews page, pulled from our public Google Business listing. This doesn't involve your personal information unless you've already chosen to leave a public review on Google.</li>
		<li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>: loads the typefaces used on this site directly from Google's servers.</li>
		<li><strong>Vercel</strong>: our website hosting provider, which processes standard web-server logs (see "Cookies &amp; Tracking" below).</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We don't use any of these services to sell your data or to build advertising profiles about you.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies &amp; Tracking</h2>
	<p>
		We don't currently use analytics or advertising cookies on this site. Our website host may
		log basic technical information (like IP address and browser type) as part of standard web
		hosting, which we don't use to identify or track individual visitors. Because we don't engage
		in this kind of tracking, our site does not currently respond differently to "Do Not Track"
		browser signals — there's no tracking to turn off.
	</p>

	<h2>Data Retention</h2>
	<p>
		We keep your information for as long as needed to provide our services, maintain our
		business, accounting, and tax records, and resolve any disputes. If you ask us to delete your
		information (see "Your Rights" below), we'll do so except where we're required or permitted
		to keep it — for example, records tied to a completed payment, which we may need to retain for
		tax and accounting purposes.
	</p>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>
		We take reasonable steps to protect your information, including relying on established
		providers (Stripe, Google) that maintain their own security programs for the payment and
		calendar data they process on our behalf, and limiting internal access to what each team
		member needs. That said, no method of storage or transmission over the internet is
		completely secure, and we can't guarantee absolute security.
	</p>

	<h2>Your Rights</h2>
	<p>
		You can reach out any time to ask what information we have about you, request a correction,
		or ask us to delete it, and we'll honor that request except where we're legally required or
		permitted to keep certain records (see "Data Retention" above). California residents may have
		additional rights under state privacy law, including the right to know what personal
		information we've collected, request its deletion, and not be discriminated against for
		exercising these rights. We don't sell or "share" personal information as those terms are
		defined under California law, so there's nothing to opt out of on that front. To make a
		request, contact us using the information below — we may need to verify your identity first.
	</p>

	<h2>Employees &amp; Job Applicants</h2>
	<p>
		This policy describes how we handle information from customers and website visitors. If
		you're a Sky House Cleaning employee or job applicant, the personal information we collect
		as part of hiring and employment (for example, through new-hire paperwork) is governed by
		separate employment policies and notices provided to you directly, not by this website
		privacy policy.
	</p>

	<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
	<p>Our services and this website are not directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect information from anyone under 13.</p>

	<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy from time to time as our services or tools change. The "last
		updated" date at the top will reflect the most recent changes. If changes are significant,
		we'll take reasonable steps to make that clear, such as noting it on this page.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact Us</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this policy or your information? Reach us at
		{" "}<a href="mailto:info@skyhousecleaning.com">info@skyhousecleaning.com</a> or
		{" "}<a href="tel:+18017592044">(801) 759-2044</a>.
	</p>
</PolicyLayout>
